# Expanded Readable Workspace

Status: DONE
Milestone: Q1 Actual-use correction
Dependencies: 25_TRANSCRIPT_FIRST_THEMES.todo (reference-only), 39_INSTALLED_CLI_ANSWERS.todo (reference-only)

## Purpose

Address the owner's rejected small, scroll-heavy, low-contrast presentation of the working tool.

## Tasks

- [x] Double requested window dimensions and clamp them to the active monitor's work area.
- [x] Use reading columns and flexible content rows rather than nested main-pane scrolling.
- [x] Make transcript/answer reading white in dark mode and black in light/neutral modes.
- [x] Keep text opaque, themes/cursor/notes/source identity and one-HWND protection policy intact.
- [x] Answer/Q&A reading surfaces share the Background slider; no opaque container blocks their transparency.
- [x] Move verbose compatibility detail behind deliberate inline Details; preserve actionable errors.
- [x] Exercise normal/minimum/resized layout and update actual synthetic illustrations.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Primary actions and useful reading space remain reachable at supported dimensions.
- [x] Foregrounds are exact high-contrast colors; unlimited content is not promised to fit a finite display.
- [x] No default-focus regression, data loss, permission prompt or unprotected popup is introduced.

